<title>UK: Baltic Handy Index fell two points to 1,097.</title>
<headline>Baltic Handy Index fell two points to 1,097.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Handy Index for Handy size shipping rates fell to 1,097 on Thursday from 1,099 on April 10, with the base being Jan 7 1997 equals 1000. The BHI is</p>
<p>based on the following routes with rates in dollars/tonne.</p>
<p> Route					 Weighting   Average   Prev</p>
<p>								   ($/Day)</p>
<p>1. Continent/Far East			 25 pct    13,290  13,150</p>
<p>2. Japan-S.Korea/NoPac or Australia RV  30	   9,100   9,125</p>
<p>3. Singapore/Australia/Continent	  15	   5,760   5,775</p>
<p>4. Continent/N or S.Atlantic RV	   30	   8,638   8,750</p>
<p>(All for 43,000 DWT)</p>
<p>Ongoing Trial Routes					     $/MT</p>
<p>T1 1.4-1.6 M 55' USG/Continent-Grains    -	    15.50  15.50</p>
<p>T2 28/32,000 53' Brazil/Continent-Grains -	    18.75  18.75</p>
<p>Note - The Index initially to be published each Tuesday and</p>
<p>Thursday is derived from four Handymax time charter routes based</p>
<p>on the 'Baltic Handy Max', a modern 43,000 DWT vessel with 25</p>
<p>ton cranes.  The Baltic Exchange will also publish returns on</p>
<p>two other trial routes alongside the Index. They may be included</p>
<p>in it at a later date.</p>
</text>
